# M0 walkthrough: health, auth and device tokens.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the JetBrains HTTP client.
# Paste your SUPERAGENT_ADMIN_TOKEN from .env below. Don't commit it.
# Dev server: http://127.0.0.1:4111. Packaged stack (pnpm stack:up): http://127.0.0.1:4112.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:4111
@token = paste-your-admin-token-here

### Liveness (public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Readiness (public, checks Postgres)
GET {{baseUrl}}/ready

### No token: 401 problem+json
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/me

### Who am I
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a device token. The secret appears only in this response.
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "laptop" }

### List tokens (prefixes only, never secrets)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Use the new token
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{created.response.body.token}}

### Tokens also work as ?apiKey= (for EventSource clients)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/me?apiKey={{created.response.body.token}}

### Revoke it (204). Using it again returns 401.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/tokens/{{created.response.body.record.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Validation errors are problem+json with field details (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Mastra runtime routes live under /api. The agent list stays empty until M2.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/agents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### OpenAPI document (public in dev, token required in production)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/openapi.json

# Interactive docs (dev only): open {{baseUrl}}/v1/docs in a browser.
